WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.440 --> 00:00:05.050
Long before it hit theaters, Avengers: Infinity
War had Marvel fans guessing who would live,

00:00:05.050 --> 00:00:10.030
who would die, and what would happen if, and
when, Thanos got his hands on the Infinity

00:00:10.030 --> 00:00:11.030
Stones.

00:00:11.030 --> 00:00:15.070
Now that the movie’s out, though, the speculation
hasn’t stopped, and some fans have a new

00:00:15.070 --> 00:00:19.950
theory that might change everything… in
the unlikely event that it’s actually true.

00:00:19.950 --> 00:00:24.360
If you haven’t seen Infinity War yet, be
careful: we’re about to get into some deep

00:00:24.360 --> 00:00:26.110
spoiler territory.

00:00:26.110 --> 00:00:30.680
One of the most shocking moments of the film
comes right at the start, when Thanos kills

00:00:30.680 --> 00:00:33.829
Loki, Thor’s occasionally supervillainous
brother.

00:00:33.829 --> 00:00:37.629
It certainly seems like a definitive end to
Tom Hiddleston’s fan-favorite character,

00:00:37.629 --> 00:00:42.211
but since we’ve seen Loki die before and
return through trickery and illusions, a few

00:00:42.211 --> 00:00:46.309
moviegoers are wondering if there might be
something more than meets the eye going on

00:00:46.309 --> 00:00:47.309
here.

00:00:47.309 --> 00:00:51.879
A new theory brought up by journalist Josh
L. Dickey, mapped out in detail by ScreenRant's

00:00:51.879 --> 00:00:55.249
Thomas Bacon, suggests that Loki didn't actually
die.

00:00:55.249 --> 00:00:59.629
Instead, he's alive and well, and masquerading
as Bruce Banner.

00:00:59.629 --> 00:01:03.649
Dickey notes that "Loki's dagger sneak attack
on Thanos was feeble.

00:01:03.649 --> 00:01:07.940
He knew it wouldn't work,” suggesting that
the whole thing was a ruse to allow Loki to

00:01:07.940 --> 00:01:09.730
sneak back onto Earth.

00:01:09.730 --> 00:01:13.440
Further evidence comes from the view that
aside from not being able to turn into the

00:01:13.440 --> 00:01:18.550
Hulk, there was something a little bit off
about Banner in the rest of the movie.

00:01:18.550 --> 00:01:19.550
"I don’t know.

00:01:19.550 --> 00:01:23.390
Maybe the fact that I was trapped for two
years inside of a monster made me a little

00:01:23.390 --> 00:01:24.240
weird!"

00:01:25.490 --> 00:01:30.020
According to the theory, he’s particularly
odd in his passion-less interactions with

00:01:30.030 --> 00:01:34.340
Black Widow It’s been a few years since
their romance was teased in Avengers: Age

00:01:34.340 --> 00:01:39.460
of Ultron, but since Banner doesn’t remember
the years he spent as the Hulk, those memories

00:01:39.460 --> 00:01:41.150
should be pretty fresh in his mind.

00:01:41.150 --> 00:01:45.840
The theory also posits that Banner's inner
struggle with Hulk may actually be down to

00:01:45.840 --> 00:01:50.710
Loki disguising himself as the super-smart
scientist but being unwilling to impersonate

00:01:50.710 --> 00:01:55.200
the not-so-jolly giant, thanks to their somewhat
contentious history with each other.

00:02:02.909 --> 00:02:07.020
Dickey also suggests that this might be the
reason why Banner landed directly in Doctor

00:02:07.030 --> 00:02:10.440
Strange's Sanctum Sanctorum when he returned
to Earth.

00:02:10.440 --> 00:02:14.780
Loki has encountered the Master of the Mystic
Arts before, so it's possible that he may

00:02:14.780 --> 00:02:19.470
have directed his path from outer space towards
Doctor Strange, knowing he’d be a quality

00:02:19.470 --> 00:02:22.260
choice to spearhead the fight against Thanos.

00:02:22.260 --> 00:02:27.720
If all this is true, it could mean that the
Hulk wasn’t even on the Asgardian refugee

00:02:27.720 --> 00:02:32.830
ship at the start of Infinity War, escaping
with Valkyrie, the breakout character of Thor:

00:02:32.830 --> 00:02:36.319
Ragnarok who’s expected to return in a future
MCU film.

00:02:36.319 --> 00:02:39.650
The only problem is that, well, it’s probably
not true at all.

00:02:39.650 --> 00:02:45.459
If you take Occam’s Razor to the Loki-As-Banner
theory, you’ll find there’s a much simpler

00:02:45.459 --> 00:02:47.720
explanation for all of its points.

00:02:47.720 --> 00:02:52.550
For starters, by the time Thanos shows up
on the Asgardian ship, he’s already dealt

00:02:52.550 --> 00:02:55.160
with Loki before, and knows how he operates.

00:02:55.160 --> 00:03:00.050
He’d be prepared for and expecting deceptive
tactics like illusions and shapeshifting.

00:03:00.050 --> 00:03:04.580
Second, and probably most importantly, Banner’s
struggles with the Hulk make a lot more sense

00:03:04.580 --> 00:03:10.020
as Banner actually struggling with the Hulk
rather than Loki working a long con on the

00:03:10.020 --> 00:03:11.050
Avengers.

00:03:11.050 --> 00:03:14.710
The Hulk’s encounter with Thanos marks the
first time that the Green Goliath has been

00:03:14.710 --> 00:03:19.620
so easily defeated in a fight, which would
shatter his confidence and explain why he’s

00:03:19.620 --> 00:03:21.540
so unwilling to make a return.

00:03:21.540 --> 00:03:25.940
Also, there are several scenes in Infinity
War where Banner attempts to turn into the

00:03:25.940 --> 00:03:27.950
Hulk when no one is around to see it.

00:03:27.950 --> 00:03:33.280
That would only make sense for Loki if he
suddenly had Deadpool levels of fourth wall-breaking

00:03:33.280 --> 00:03:34.280
self-awareness.

00:03:34.280 --> 00:03:39.880
Banner’s arrival at the Sanctum Sanctorum
is pretty easy to explain away with magic,

00:03:39.880 --> 00:03:44.030
but probably happened because that scene is
lifted from the original comics.

00:03:44.030 --> 00:03:48.950
The only difference is that there, it’s
the Silver Surfer who ruins Strange’s staircase,

00:03:48.950 --> 00:03:53.220
but since he doesn’t currently exist in
the MCU, Banner makes a fitting substitute.

00:03:53.220 --> 00:03:57.780
As for Banner’s encounter with Black Widow,
there actually is some tension there, but

00:03:57.780 --> 00:03:59.050
it’s certainly not the focus.

00:03:59.050 --> 00:04:04.000
That, however, is easily explained by the
fact that the romance teased in Age of Ultron

00:04:04.000 --> 00:04:06.510
wasn’t exactly the best part of that movie.

00:04:06.510 --> 00:04:10.430
Some viewers felt like it came out of nowhere,
and didn’t really serve either character

00:04:10.430 --> 00:04:13.959
well, so it makes sense that the next film
might downplay it.

00:04:13.959 --> 00:04:17.100
Or maybe Bruce Banner just doesn’t prefer
blondes.

00:04:17.100 --> 00:04:18.100
Thanks for watching!

